<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Musical setting by Narayan Khare at Sabarmati</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1920s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new tune in Mishra Khamaj, now the best known</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Narsi Bhagat (Vijay Bhatt)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1940</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung at the film's close</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gandhi (Richard Attenborough)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">under the closing titles</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English prose version in the Ashram Bhajanavali (Mahatma Gandhi)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1928–1930</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English version with commentary (Mahatma Gandhi), lost</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1920</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Navajivan articles against untouchability (Mahatma Gandhi)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Narasinha Mehta, Uttam Pado (Asit Desai, Hema Desai)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Riyaaz Qawwali</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as a qawwali with couplets of Kabir</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Vaishnava Jana To (Brodha V)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">refrain used in a hip-hop single</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gujarati exegesis for the Gurjarvani centre (Vinayak Jadav, S.J.)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">commentary illustrating Christian ideals</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Premodern Gujarati poems defining a Vaishnava in ethical terms</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the tradition it belongs to (Shukla-Bhatt)</span></li></ul></section>
